      "writtenOn": "2024-03-07T02:01:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "we need to be careful here also because calls to kobject_uevent_env() are also potentially sleeping.  how about something like\n\nspin_lock()\nif (opts-\u003econnected !\u003d opts-\u003esw_connected) {\n\t\tif (opts-\u003econnected)\n\t\t\tconnected \u003d true;\n\t\telse\n\t\t\tdisconnected \u003d true;\n\t\topts-\u003esw_connected \u003d opts-\u003econnected;\n\t}\n\tif (opts-\u003econfigured)\n\t\tconfigured \u003d true;\nspin_unlock()\n\nthen below you operate purely on the local variables that were determined based on the opt parameters.  at least that way, state changes are not intermixed. (ie if a state change occurred while reading in it in the worker thread)  if the state changes after this point, that is fine, as the state change API will schedule_work() to run this routine again and we would propagate the new USB connection state as a separate uevent.",
      "revId": "e53a610d10b0561c09d31f88dc658dad9a00a9fc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
