      "writtenOn": "2024-03-07T03:24:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You are correct- the intent was to unlock and operate on the local configured variables. The reason for keeping the lock around until after the uevents are sent is so the dev doesn\u0027t get destroyed while we are accessing it. I started to play with incrementing the dev\u0027s reference count in the lock with get_device(), storing a pointer to it, unlocking, sending the uevents, then calling put_device(), but realized the logic around android_device_destroy() wouldn\u0027t support this.",
      "parentUuid": "7977ab9c_1ea12df7",
      "revId": "e53a610d10b0561c09d31f88dc658dad9a00a9fc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
